In ES2015 (ES6), we can use template literals instead of string concatenation.
```
var str = `Hello, ${name}!`;
```

### Bad Practice

```js
var str = "Hello, " + name + "!";
var str = "Time: " + (12 * 60 * 60 * 1000);
```

### Recommended

```js
var str = "Hello World!";
var str = `Hello, ${name}!`;
var str = `Time: ${12 * 60 * 60 * 1000}`;

var str = "Hello, " + "World!";
```

